      "id": "DC1",
      "label": "Diagnostic Criteria",
      "name": "Diagnostic Requirements for Episode of harmful use of opioids",
      "properties": {
        "required_core_symptoms": "An episode of use of opioids that has caused clinically significant damage to a person’s physical health or mental health, or has resulted in behaviour leading to harm to the health of others. Harm to health of the individual occurs due to behaviour related to intoxication, direct or secondary toxic effects on body organs and systems, or a harmful route of administration.",
        "functional_impairment_requirements": "clinically significant damage to a person’s physical health or mental health, or has resulted in behaviour leading to harm to the health of others",
        "exclusion_details": "Harm to health is not better accounted for by another medical condition or another mental disorder, including another Disorder Due to Substance Use. This diagnosis should not be made if the harm is attributed to a known pattern of opioid use."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
