      "id": "DC1",
      "label": "Diagnostic Criteria",
      "name": "Diagnostic Requirements for Episode of Harmful Use of Cocaine",
      "properties": {
        "required_core_symptoms": "An episode of use of cocaine that has caused clinically significant damage to a person’s physical health or mental health, or has resulted in behaviour leading to harm to the health of others. Harm occurs due to behaviour related to intoxication, direct or secondary toxic effects, or a harmful route of administration. Clear causal relationship between the harm to health and the episode of cocaine use.",
        "functional_impairment_requirements": "Clinically significant harm to the individual’s physical or mental health or that of others.",
        "exclusion_details": "Harm to health is not better accounted for by another medical condition or another mental disorder. This diagnosis should not be made if the harm is attributed to a known pattern of cocaine use."
      }
