      "label": "Diagnostic Criteria",
      "name": "Diagnostic Criteria for Kleptomania",
      "properties": {
        "required_core_symptoms": "A recurrent failure to control strong impulses to steal objects; Lack of an apparent motive for stealing objects; increased tension or affective arousal prior to instances of theft; pleasure, excitement, relief, or gratification during and immediately following the act of stealing.",
        "exclusion_details": "Acts of theft or attempted theft are not better accounted for by a Disorder of Intellectual Development, another mental disorder (e.g., a Manic Episode), or Substance Intoxication. Individuals who steal for monetary gain due to the financial implications of their substance use or gambling should not be diagnosed with Kleptomania."
